The legal texts are laws of the Republic of the Philippines as published in the Official Gazette
(https://www.officialgazette.gov.ph), whose site states: "All content is in the public domain unless otherwise
stated." Under Republic Act No. 8293 (Intellectual Property Code), section 176, no copyright subsists in any work
of the Government of the Philippines.

Changes made by Lexifina: each law was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per line;
chapter and article headings were left out of the units; five evident transcription errors in the Official
Gazette's page of the Constitution were corrected. The versions were arranged as git commits.
Lexifina does not claim the Official Gazette endorses this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the
tools) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
